  "instructions": [
    "Preheat oven to 375°F (190°C).",
    "Roll out empanada dough to a thickness of about 1/8 inch (3mm).",
    "Cut out circles of dough using a cookie cutter or the rim of a glass.",
    "Place a tablespoon or two of the beef mixture onto the center of each dough circle.",
    "Brush the edges of the dough with water.",
    "Fold the dough over the filling to form a half-circle shape, pressing the edges together to seal.",
    "Use a fork to crimp the edges.",
    "Brush the tops of the empanadas with olive oil.",
    "Place the empanadas on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper.",
    "Bake for 20-25 minutes, or until the empanadas are golden brown.",
    "Serve warm."
